<section class="section"><div class="container article-body">
<h2>DQ Caramel Sundae — The Sweet, Buttery Option</h2>
<p>Dairy Queen's signature caramel sauce boasts a thick, glossy consistency that clings beautifully to cold vanilla soft serve. Unlike warmer fudge that tends to run straight to the bottom of the dish, this buttery caramel ribbon wraps itself around every curve of soft serve, delivering consistent flavor from your very first spoonful down to the final bite. Discover all of our nostalgic frozen recipes on <a href="/">The Queen Dairy Menu</a>.</p>
<h2>Caramel vs. Hot Fudge Sundae — Which to Choose?</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Caramel Sundae</strong> — Sweeter, more viscous, buttery flavor profile. Best for caramel fans and guests who prefer a lighter, non-chocolate dessert.</li>
  <li><strong>Hot Fudge Sundae</strong> — Rich chocolate, warm-cold temperature contrast. Best for chocolate fans who want the classic sundae experience.</li>
  <li>Both are $3.79. Choose based on flavor preference — chocolate or caramel. Both are excellent value at the same price.</li>
</ul>
<h2>Caramel Sundae in the DQ Value Lineup</h2>
<p>Value-conscious diners will be thrilled to know that the Caramel Sundae is one of the premier dessert options you can choose inside the famous <a href="/items/7-meal-deal">$7 Meal Deal</a>. If you order it à la carte at $3.79, it still provides exceptional value for a premium dessert, matching the price of basic french fries while providing an indulgent, ice-cream parlor finish to any lunch or dinner.</p>
<h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
<div class="faq-list"><div class="faq-item"><button class="faq-q" aria-expanded="false">How much is the DQ Caramel Sundae?<span class="faq-icon">+</span></button><div class="faq-a"><div class="faq-a-inner">A standard DQ Caramel Sundae costs $3.79 and contains approximately 310 calories.</div></div></div><div class="faq-item"><button class="faq-q" aria-expanded="false">Is the Caramel Sundae available at every DQ?<span class="faq-icon">+</span></button><div class="faq-a"><div class="faq-a-inner">Yes! Because caramel topping and vanilla soft serve are fundamental staples, this sundae is served year-round across all DQ restaurants, walk-ups, and mall locations.</div></div></div><div class="faq-item"><button class="faq-q" aria-expanded="false">Can I get caramel and hot fudge on the same sundae?<span class="faq-icon">+</span></button><div class="faq-a"><div class="faq-a-inner">Yes, most crews are happy to make it! Asking for both caramel and hot fudge gives you a customized "Turtle-style" sundae, typically for a small topping upcharge (~$0.50).</div></div></div></div>
<p style="margin-top:32px;">For the complete DQ menu with all categories and deals, visit <a href="/"><strong>The Queen Dairy Menu</strong></a>.</p>
</div></section>
<section class="section section-alt">
  <div class="container article-body" style="max-width:920px;">
    <h2>The Caramel Sundae — The Richest of the Three</h2>
    <p>While Dairy Queen prices all three of its foundational sundaes equally at $3.79, their taste profiles are distinct. The Caramel Sundae stands out as the sweetest and highest in calorie density at 310 calories (surpassing Hot Fudge at 300 and Strawberry at 280). Its thick caramel coating creates an irresistible buttery depth that appeals to serious dessert lovers. View our complete sweet lineup on <a href="/">The Queen Dairy Menu</a>.</p>

    <h2>Three DQ Sundaes Side by Side</h2>
    <div class="table-wrap"><table class="size-table">
      <thead><tr><th>Sundae</th><th>Price</th><th>Calories</th><th>Flavor Profile</th><th>Best For</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td><strong>Caramel Sundae</strong></td><td class="price-cell">$3.79</td><td>310</td><td>Buttery sweet caramel</td><td>Rich dessert fans</td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong><a href="/items/hot-fudge-sundae">Hot Fudge Sundae</a></strong></td><td class="price-cell">$3.79</td><td>300</td><td>Warm chocolate</td><td>Classic chocolate lovers</td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong><a href="/items/strawberry-sundae">Strawberry Sundae</a></strong></td><td class="price-cell">$3.79</td><td>280</td><td>Fruity strawberry</td><td>Lighter, fruit-forward</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table></div>

    <h2>When to Order the Caramel Sundae</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>When you want maximum sweetness:</strong> Caramel is the sweetest of the three toppings. If you have a strong sweet tooth, caramel delivers more than fudge or strawberry.</li>
      <li><strong>After a salty meal:</strong> The salty-sweet contrast is one of the great food pairings. The Caramel Sundae after a <a href="/items/chicken-strip-basket-4pc">Chicken Strip Basket</a> or <a href="/items/chili-cheese-dog">Chili Cheese Dog</a> works particularly well for this reason.</li>
      <li><strong>As a $7 Meal Deal dessert:</strong> The Caramel Sundae is eligible as the Small Sundae in the <a href="/items/7-meal-deal">$7 Meal Deal</a> — the richest dessert you can get within that deal.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Caramel Sundae vs. Peanut Buster Parfait</h2>
    <p>If you're seeking even deeper decadence, you might compare this to the legendary <a href="/items/peanut-buster-parfait">Peanut Buster Parfait</a> ($4.99, 710 cal). While the Parfait layers hot fudge and salty peanuts for maximum texture, the Caramel Sundae keeps the focus purely on sweet, buttery simplicity. At $3.79, it delivers classic sundae pleasure at a fraction of the cost and calories.</p>

    <h2>Ordering Tips</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Eat immediately:</strong> Caramel sauce warms the soft serve faster than strawberry. The texture is best in the first two minutes.</li>
      <li><strong>Request extra caramel:</strong> Available at most locations for a small upcharge. Worthwhile if you want more sauce coverage.</li>
      <li><strong>Consider the Banana Split alternative:</strong> The <a href="/items/banana-split">Banana Split</a> ($5.69) includes caramel as one of its three toppings alongside pineapple and strawberry — a more complex option for $1.90 more.</li>
    </ul>

